8,0$ Fruitbodies attached by a whitish rooting base, often distinctly but shortly stipitate, with a mushroom-shaped head, ranging from concave to convex ; spores elliptic to allantoid, (9-) tOD-I 3-75 x 4 0-5 3 (-6-2) µm, the septa either thin or slightly thickened $ D. capitatus
