10,0$Type species: Dacrymyces stillatus Nees ex Fr.///The generic limits of Dacrymyces are not sharply defined, the speciestend to grade toward Ditiola from the one hand and more positively toward Guepiniopsis Pat. /// on the other. Species of Dacrymyces may be distinguished from those of Ditiola in having a homogenous composition of the fruit body. The only British species liable to cause trouble in this  respect is Dacrymyces capitatus Schw. Members of the genus Guepiniopsis  are distinguished from cupulate species of Dacrymyces in having the sterile  surfaces covered by a palisade of cortical hairs which are usually c1early  differentiated from the vegetative hyphae. Here the ethic source of  trouble is G. chrysocoma (Bull. ex St Amans) Brasf. which has the palisadic  structure referred to above but the cortical hairs of which it is composed  are relatively unspecialized.
12,0$Göttel G (1983) Untersuchungen zur Systematik der Gattung Dacrymyces Nees per Fr. (Basidiomycetes). 